## [v0.6.9 – Admin Metrics Dashboard]
**Date:** 2025-12-21

### Changes Made:
- Created admin-only `/metrics` page with real-time analytics dashboard
- Added backend metrics handler with `GET /admin/metrics/overview` and `GET /admin/metrics/charts` endpoints
- Implemented aggregate stats: user counts (total, verified, by period), task counts (total, active, completed, avg duration), session stats (total time tracked, active now)
- Added top 10 users leaderboard ranked by time tracked
- Created time-series chart data with configurable periods (week/month/year) and metrics (signups/tasks/sessions/time)
- Installed Recharts library for responsive line charts with tooltips
- Added admin middleware protection for metrics endpoints (403 for non-admin users)
- Implemented 30-second polling for real-time dashboard updates
- Added Metrics link to profile dropdown (admin-only visibility)
- Created comprehensive backend tests (18 tests) covering access control, data counts, and chart endpoints
- Created frontend API tests (16 tests) for metricsApi service
- Created frontend component tests (14 tests) for metrics page

### Files Created:
- `backend/internal/models/metrics.go` - Type definitions for metrics responses
- `backend/internal/handlers/metrics.go` - API handlers for overview and chart data
- `backend/internal/handlers/metrics_test.go` - Backend handler tests
- `frontend/src/services/metricsApi.ts` - Frontend API client
- `frontend/src/services/metricsApi.test.ts` - API client tests
- `frontend/src/app/metrics/page.tsx` - Admin metrics dashboard page
- `frontend/src/app/metrics/metrics.css` - Dashboard styles
- `frontend/src/app/metrics/metrics.test.tsx` - Page component tests

### Files Modified:
- `backend/cmd/server/main.go` - Added metricsHandler and admin routes
- `frontend/package.json` - Added recharts dependency
- `frontend/src/components/header/Header.tsx` - Added Metrics link for admins

### Current Status:
All features working. Backend and frontend build successfully. All 48 new metrics tests pass. Dashboard displays user stats, task stats, session time tracking, trend charts, and top users table. Admin-only access enforced at both API and UI levels.

